<Base title="About the Project — ACTA FRAGILIA" description="Independent platform for analytical journalism, investigations and documentary analysis.">
  <main class="about-page">
    <h1>About the Project</h1>

    <p><strong>ACTA FRAGILIA is an independent platform for analytical journalism, investigations and documentary analysis in the fields of law, economics, corporate conflicts and social processes.</strong></p>

    <p>No advertising, news feed or noise. Only verified facts, context and an attempt to understand how legal, economic and social mechanisms work — and who bears their consequences.</p>

    <h2>Principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fact-checking.</strong> Every claim is verified against primary sources.</li>
      <li><strong>Context over sensation.</strong> We analyze systemic causes, not isolated cases.</li>
      <li><strong>Attention to consequences.</strong> We ask: who bears the cost of decisions made?</li>
      <li><strong>No news cycle pressure.</strong> Texts are published when they are ready, not when the news agenda demands.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Methodology</h2>
    <p>Materials are based on court documents, regulatory filings, corporate registries and direct interviews. Where possible, we publish links to sources or scans of documents.</p>

    <h2>Languages</h2>
    <p>The project publishes in Russian, English, Polish, Belarusian and Ukrainian. Not all materials are available in all languages — priority is given to the language most relevant to the subject.</p>
  </main>
</Base>

